program block_dedent_warning

? A same-indent statement after an indented body still belongs to the block:
? only `$` closes it (the compiler warns about the dedent). This locks in
? that semantics: the guarded lines below do NOT run, so x stays 5.

@ main ||:
	expected: []
	expected.push|"5"|

	x: 5
	if x is 99 then
		y: x + 1
		print|y|
	x = x + 10
	print|x|
	$
	print|x|
	print|expected|
$
